<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eschnerberg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eschnerberg is a low, wooded ridge in the Unterland of Liechtenstein, rising above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> valley. Inhabited since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a>, it carried the castles of the Schellenberg family in the 13th century, and villages of the former Lordship of Schellenberg, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eschen">Eschen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamprin">Gamprin</a> and Schellenberg, lie on its slopes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eschnerberg.jpg" alt="Eschnerberg" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Plutowiki · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eschnerberg_von_West.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
